<title>MEXICO: Weekly Mexican export, import feeder summary -USDA.</title>
<headline>Weekly Mexican export, import feeder summary -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Friday that numbers of steer calves exported to the United States from Mexico were not sufficient to establish quote prices.</p>
<p>Exports for the week were estimated at 3,000 head into Texas and New Mexico against 5,843 head last week and 5,342 head in the same week in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;Around 90 percent of supply were previously contracted, sold on video...&quot; USDA said. &quot;Bulk of supply consisted of steers weighing 300-600 lb,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>Imports into Mexico of slaughter cattle were estimated to have totaled 3,000 head for the week, it added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530)). E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
</text>
